From: "Caleb J. Westfall" <calebwestfall1989@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 09:21:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ProofScope v1.0: Assumption Delta, boundary witness
 synthesis, Mathlib track

- AssumptionDelta.lean: an added assumption changes the claim iff a model of
  the reference conditions violates it (restrictive_iff_strictly_weaker);
  redundancy, necessity, dichotomy, polarity and domain theorems
- AssumptionExtract.lean + adelta.py: telescope alignment, certified
  redundant/restrictive/necessary obligations, witness models read from
  kernel-checked proof terms
- BoundarySynth.lean + cmcd_v10.py: boundary interpretations for comparison
  changes (wraps the frozen v0.9 engine); blind b13/b14 now certified
- Block-1 frozen run found an Assumption Delta soundness bug (model scope;
  x01 wrong, ad02 unsound); fixed in block 2 (v1.0.2), documented
- Mathlib track workflow (pinned d13f23b) with 8 cases: PENDING first run

